# Loaded automatically by Firebase Functions v2 only when running against the
# `demo-trivimind-local` project — i.e. only inside the local emulator that
# `npm start` and `npm run firebase:emulate` start. Never a real deploy.
# Safe to commit: not a secret, just a feature flag.
#
# Its twin is `.env.demo-trivia-app-e2e`, which does the same job for the e2e
# suite. Two files rather than one shared project id, so an e2e run — which
# wipes emulator state between specs — cannot empty the data you were
# developing against.
#
# Skips real Stripe API calls entirely in createCheckoutSession (see
# src/checkout-sessions.ts) and writes back a deterministic fake session
# instead, so local development never needs real Stripe credentials.
STRIPE_MOCK_CHECKOUT=true
